Workstream ID: encrypted-progress-journal
Title: Optional encrypted append-only repository progress journal
Status: DONE
Milestone: Manual cross-browser progress publication on GitHub static Pages
Dependencies: tracker-foundation
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/CareerOS/issues/7
Purpose: Record the separate browser-encrypted export/publication workflow while
  preserving ordinary backups, imports, reset, schemas and all existing features.
  This feature is unrelated to development TODO-to-GitHub tracking.

Tasks:
  [x] Add separate Settings entry and repository-sync route.
  [x] Encrypt baseline/deltas with a session-only key and authenticated metadata.
  [x] Validate append chains, duplicate IDs, size limits and rollback boundaries.
  [x] Keep an encrypted local outbox and require actual deployed-file acknowledgment.
  [x] Review first connections/incompatible changes instead of silently overwriting.
  [x] Preserve original browser saving, backups, tutorial isolation and recovery.
  [x] Add focused unit/browser coverage and document privacy/passphrase limitations.

Acceptance criteria:
  Entirely static: no backend, embedded GitHub credential or automatic publication.
  Only a successful same-origin deployed-file load acknowledges publication.
  Local unpublished work, conflicts and non-atomic storage failures are explicit.
  The public journal ships empty; no actual workspace/passphrase is published.
  Original plaintext full backups remain available as a separate existing feature.

